WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.990
Broadcast channels, cable networks, and streaming
services have unveiled their next wave of

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.760
new and returning shows, and there's a lot
to look forward to.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.760
But not every series can be a hit.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.580
Will your new favorite guilty pleasure thrive,
or will it even survive the year?

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.500
Here's a look at some new TV shows that probably
won't survive 2018.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.420
Living Biblically

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.280
In 2007, humorist A.J.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.620
Jacobs made waves with his book My Year of
Living Biblically, in which he tried to live

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.120
every aspect of his life according to the
rules set forth in the Bible.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.920
Now, the book has been adapted as a gimmicky
sitcom.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.640
Jay R. Ferguson, hot off of the quickly-cancelled
sitcom The Real O'Neals, plays Chip Curry,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.290
a guy at a crossroads in his life: After the
death of a friend and with a baby on the way,

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.020
he freaks out and opts to live, you know,
biblically.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.480
It could be funny, but for whom?

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.780
Living Biblically risks offending true believers,
but the subject matter could also easily alienate

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:52.790
non-religious viewers.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.700
That's a tough balancing act, so something
will have to give.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.020
"So when God says 'Do not worship false idols,'
he's talking about Beyonce."

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:02.500
Rise

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.520
An idealistic teacher at a cash-strapped school
is determined to put on a musical and show

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.620
his students the power of their dreams.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.360
You'd expect Rise to be inspiring.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.840
Instead, it's oddly depressing, despite featuring
How I Met Your Mother's Josh Radnor and boasting

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.530
a bunch of supposedly uplifting musical numbers.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.479
Glee proved that something like Rise could
be good, but so far, it's too earnest for

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.180
its own good.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.100
Unless it learns how to lighten up, Rise may
soon fall.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.240
"This isn't just about your vision, Mr. Mazzu.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.420
These are people's lives you're dealing with."

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.240
American Idol

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.240
It was once the most popular TV show in the
world.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.539
But just two short years ago, fans had become
so burned out on American Idol that it was

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:44.520
unceremoniously dumped by Fox.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.509
Now it's back on ABC, but in a world dominated
by NBC's The Voice, do fans even want more

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.320
American Idol?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.580
Sure, it boasts Katy Perry at the head of
a new lineup of judges, but it also features

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.749
the return of embattled host Ryan Seacrest,
who has become something of a Hollywood pariah

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:01.009
after accusations of harassment surfaced.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.469
He was later cleared by a network investigation,
but just like nobody was asking for the show

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:08.620
to return, nobody was asking for Seacrest
to return either.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.500
It's just not a good way to start what was
bound to be an uphill climb for American idol

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.000
anyway.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.640
Titans

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.480
There have been a lot of shows based around
Teen Titans, the scrappy DC Comics property

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:24.260
about the adventures of a squad of young superheroes
and erstwhile sidekicks, which at various

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:29.620
times has included characters like Robin,
Kid Flash, Aqualad, Raven, and Starfire.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.510
But while the animated versions of Teen Titans
have been popular over the years, the new

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.159
live action Titans has had a very troubled
development.

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:40.129
TNT announced the show in 2014 but the pilot
never materialized.

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:45.060
Instead, the team behind the popular line
of DC shows on The CW announced a new version

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.469
in 2017… but it's not going to be on The
CW, instead debuting at an undetermined date

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:54.360
on DC's upcoming streaming service - which
doesn't actually exist yet.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.040
It's going to take some real superheroics
to save this one.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:58.680
Heathers

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.500
A TV series is almost certainly doomed to
fail if it never actually airs, right?

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:08.190
The Paramount Network's TV adaptation of the
1988 high school black comedy Heathers is

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.939
looking like it could enter the rare gallery
of shows canceled before they broadcast a

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.920
single episode.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.480
Scheduled to debut in early March, Heathers
was delayed indefinitely due to the Parkland,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.780
Florida school shooting.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.780
Taking Heathers off the table was a move made
out of good taste.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:26.400
Like its 1988 cult classic source material,
it's a story about getting back at bullies

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.500
through school violence.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.620
Daniel D'addario of Time said the series "makes
broad and sloppy comedy out of the idea of

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.060
teens dying, by their own hand or at the hands
of other teens.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.660
It's seemingly designed to provoke and to
offend."

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.900
That might have worked 30 years ago, but it
doesn't work now.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.760
Here and Now

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.840
Created by Alan Ball, Here and Now combines
the complicated family dynamics and awareness

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.300
of his series Six Feet Under, with the kooky
supernaturalism of his other series, True

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:53.800
Blood.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.180
The result is less than the sum of its parts,
with Tim Robbins and Holly Hunter playing

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.680
parents to an international conglomeration
of adopted children, allowing them to have

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.160
unnaturally Important Conversations about
the Issues of Our Time.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.400
Multiple characters also have weird prophetic
dreams and spooky hallucinations, numerology

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:15.790
is an important plot device, and Robbins'
character is anxious about aging and is also

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:16.500
having an affair.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.160
In other words, Here and Now tries to be too
many things to too many people, and as a result

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.800
actually does nothing for anybody.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.360
Ratings have been terrible and critical reception
has been even worse, suggesting Here and Now

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.130
may soon be Then and Gone.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.160
Thanks for watching!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.920
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

